{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "359c090d-3474-4b10-bb60-7ddca677c050",
    "name": "SCG NetSuite Integration (RESTlet, OAuth 1.0 TBA)",
    "description": "Read-only requests for SCG's NetSuite integration RESTlet (see netsuite_api_docs/).\n\n**Setup**\n1. Import this collection and `NetSuite.postman_environment.json`.\n2. In the environment, fill `account_id` (e.g. `1234567_SB1`) and the four keys: `consumer_key`, `consumer_secret`, `token_id`, `token_secret`. Put the keys in **Current value** only, so they stay on your machine and aren't synced or exported.\n3. Select the environment and run **00 Connection test → Subsidiary list** first.\n\n**Auth** is set once on the collection: OAuth 1.0, HMAC-SHA256, realm = `account_id`. Every request inherits it.\n`account_host` (`1234567-sb1`) is derived from `account_id` by the collection pre-request script.\n\n**Responses** are always HTTP 200. The real result is `status` / `code` / `error` in the body; the collection tests check it.\nLists return `data: { total, per_page, current_page, last_page, data: [...] }`. Dates are DD/MM/YYYY.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "oauth1",
    "oauth1": [
      {
        "key": "signatureMethod",
        "value": "HMAC-SHA256",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "version",
        "value": "1.0",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "realm",
        "value": "{{account_id}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "consumerKey",
        "value": "{{consumer_key}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "consumerSecret",
        "value": "{{consumer_secret}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token_id}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "tokenSecret",
        "value": "{{token_secret}}",
        "type": "string"
      },
      {
        "key": "addParamsToHeader",
        "value": true,
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      {
        "key": "addEmptyParamsToSign",
        "value": false,
        "type": "boolean"
      },
      {
        "key": "includeBodyHash",
        "value": false,
        "type": "boolean"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// account_id 1234567_SB1 -> realm 1234567_SB1, host 1234567-sb1.restlets.api.netsuite.com",
          "const id = (pm.variables.get('account_id') || '').trim().toUpperCase().replace(/-/g, '_');",
          "if (!id) throw new Error('Set account_id in the environment (e.g. 1234567_SB1).');",
          "for (const k of ['consumer_key', 'consumer_secret', 'token_id', 'token_secret']) {",
          "  if (!pm.variables.get(k)) throw new Error(`Set ${k} in the environment (Current value).`);",
          "}",
          "pm.variables.set('account_id', id);",
          "pm.variables.set('account_host', id.toLowerCase().replace(/_/g, '-'));"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// NetSuite answers HTTP 200 even for errors; the result is in the body.",
          "pm.test('HTTP 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
          "let body;",
          "try { body = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) { body = null; }",
          "pm.test('JSON body', () => pm.expect(body, pm.response.text().slice(0, 200)).to.be.an('object'));",
          "if (body) {",
          "  const err = body.error ? `${body.error.code || ''}: ${body.error.message || JSON.stringify(body.error)}` : '';",
          "  pm.test('status = success', () => pm.expect(body.status, err).to.eql('success'));",
          "  const d = body.data;",
          "  if (d && Array.isArray(d.data)) console.log(`total=${d.total} page=${d.current_page}/${d.last_page} rows=${d.data.length}`);",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "script_id",
      "value": "customscript_int_api",
      "description": "RESTlet for endpoints #01–#41"
    },
    {
      "key": "script_id_2",
      "value": "customscript_int_api_2",
      "description": "RESTlet for endpoints #42 and later"
    },
    {
      "key": "deploy_id",
      "value": "1"
    }
  ],
